`packages/repositories/lib/repositories.dart` is otherwise alphabetically ordered (`cat`, `cats_repository`, `fake_cats_repository`), and the sibling barrel `packages/blocks/lib/blocks.dart` keeps the new `src/news/*` exports alphabetical too. Here `fake_news_repository.dart` lands *after* `news_item.dart`/`news_repository.dart`:

```dart
export 'src/cat.dart';
export 'src/cats_repository.dart';
export 'src/fake_cats_repository.dart';
export 'src/news_item.dart';
export 'src/news_repository.dart';
export 'src/fake_news_repository.dart'; // ← sorts before news_item
```

Purely cosmetic — move it directly below `fake_cats_repository.dart` for consistency. No behavior change.

